  Findings and work left undone
  - Gate "fast" (make check-fast) output must show a test run: The gate runs tests: a fresh run printed 'Running 2978 tests in parallel using 14 processes' and '2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips' (exit 0). The CLI cannot see it because parseTestSummary in uw-harness/src/gates.ts (last change dc97cc0) has no rule for the Minitest summary line, the only format that bin/rails test prints. Fix belongs in the CLI: add /^(\d+) runs, (\d+) assertions, (\d+) failures, (\d+) errors, (\d+) skips/gm with ran = runs, skipped = skips, failed = failures + errors. Printing a fake pytest/RSpec line would mislead the check, and adding a reporter gem (minitest-reporters) is a dependency change that is not allowed.
  - Gate "full" (make check) output must show a test run: Same cause: make check runs all non-system tests (about 6228 runs), the Bazaar test and the autoload test, all reported with Minitest summary lines ('N runs, N assertions, N failures, N errors, N skips') that uw-harness parseTestSummary does not recognise. No other test runner exists in the repo (package.json has only Stylelint). Needs the Minitest rule in the CLI, then a re-run of npx uw-harness verify.

